{"The working-hours check compares both start and end using the slot start time, ignoring the event length - a slot that starts before workingHour.endTime but ends after it will still be allowed incorrectly": 0.9274922609329224, "The equality check comparing dayjs objects uses === which compares object references instead of underlying date values, causing the start==end override case to always be false and incorrectly allow availability": 0.8972529172897339, "When a date override exists for the day, the function returns true before checking busy slots, which makes any slot inside a date override appear available even if the host is booked/busy, leading to potential double-booking": 0.8761435151100159, "The working-hours logic returns false if the slot is outside any workingHour for that day, so with split working hours (e.g., morning and afternoon), a slot inside one range will still be rejected because it's outside another": 0.9401638507843018, "If dateOverrideExist is false and there are no workingHours defined for the current day, the function incorrectly proceeds to check busy times, treating users as available when no working hours are defined instead of unavailable": 0.8173509836196899}